  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of life-saving medical equipment and supplies in response to the earthquake in Khoy, Iran</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The key objective of this project is to provide essential life-saving medical equipment and supplies to the health facilities that are accommodating earthquake-affected patients in Khoy. With its Health sector engagement, the project targets 3,440 patients requiring breathing support, trauma care, and cardiac life support through WHO&#x2019;s procurement and donation to health facilities of two mechanical ventilators, one trauma and emergency surgical kit (TESK), and four portable Automated External Defibrillators.</narrative>
  </description>
